  "note": "A2 liść · SECOND pack of Oxford A2 vocab-gap batch 2 (VOCAB-BUILD-DIGEST batch 2). Grouping rationale: twelve Oxford-A2 nouns for the physical world — księżyc, planeta, ocean, wybrzeże, dolina, pustynia, kontynent, skała, region, złoto, srebro, prąd. All twelve are Oxford A2 rows (moon, planet, ocean, coast, valley, desert, continent, rock, region, gold, silver, electricity); the four listed by Oxford as adjective/noun or noun/verb (gold, silver, rock, desert) are authored in their NOUN sense only, which is noted here so a later batch does not assume the adjective is covered. a1_nature already owns niebo, słońce, gwiazda, morze, jezioro, wyspa, las, góra, rzeka, ziemia, kamień, drzewo, świat — ANCHORS, never re-taught, and the pack leans on them hard (Ocean jest większy niż morze). The pack rides prep_w_loc / prep_place and the second block is a locative board, copying a2_places2's shape exactly, so teaches_structures is [] by construction. Judgment calls, all reported: (1) THE ADJECTIVE POOL, NOT THE NOUNS, DECIDED THE WORD LIST. Batch 1 flagged untaught gender forms of taught adjectives as the likeliest way a vocab pack leaks; measured properly this batch, the pool holds masculine forms for almost everything and feminine or neuter forms for only a fraction — of zimny, suchy, mokry, szary, zielony, ciekawy, niebezpieczny, ciemny, jasny, wysoki NOT ONE has a taught neuter form, and only wysoka, spokojna, zimna, gorąca survive in the feminine. drewno, metal, gaz and zanieczyszczenie were dropped from the draft list for exactly this reason — three neuters were already at the limit of what can be said about them — and the surviving neuters (wybrzeże, złoto, srebro) are described with duże / małe / nowe / droższe / tańsze, which are the neuter forms the pool actually has. (2) na Księżycu IS CAPITALISED and its explain says why: as the name of our moon it is a proper noun in Polish, the same rule that gives Polska a capital and polska książka none. That rule is already taught as content by a2_countries, so this is a recycled fact rather than a new one. (3) THE PREPOSITION IS PART OF THE LEXICAL ITEM, not derivable. na Księżycu, na wybrzeżu and na pustyni take na; w oceanie, w dolinie and w regionie take w. Nothing in the meaning predicts the split, so the block teaches the whole phrase and the explain tells the learner to take each one whole — the same treatment a2_places2 gives na dachu against w kościele. (4) dużo + genitive plural (dużo ryb, dużo parków) WAS CHECKED BEFORE USE rather than assumed: the course already ships 56 instances of it, so it is recycled, not introduced. (5) NO ICONS EXCEPT 🌙. 🌊 was drafted for ocean and cut because it reads as morze or woda, both already taught; the desert and mountain emoji carry variation selectors of the kind a2_countries found not to render on Win10. 🌙 is Emoji 1.0, unambiguous, and the only word in the pack it can point at. (6) NO PLURALS. planety, oceany, doliny and skały would all be new forms, and skały and doliny are the AGENTS.md homograph shape exactly — identical to the genitive singular — so a pack that has no need of them does not open the question.",
